VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different ways to use reference images. To show you what they all do, first up is the original method from last week using the native Kwen Image Edit Plus node.'

[12:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For the image, I\'m loading up this rodent sitting in a chair, but for the prompt, I\'m changing it up a bit so he gets a yellow optical faceplate a window out onto the city, and the posters should say obey.'

[12:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'That seems to work nicely. This way we\'re getting a new version of the image with him still wearing his little hat and the purple chair, which weren\'t in the prompt, but also with the window, posters, and his optical faceplate.'

[12:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Next is the Create 2 Image Edit Rebalance node, which as you can see from the label at the top is from the Conditioning Create 2 Rebalance Custom Node pack. This one\'s a bit different in'

[12:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that not only can it take in up to four image inputs, so that\'s one more than Kwen, but here is an optional negative prompt input as well. And if that isn\'t enough, each individual image can have'

[13:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'its own weight set at the moment to normal for each of the token values. The other options you get are low, high, and max, all helping you to get that perfect balance in your image'

[13:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'composition. Probably the first thing you notice is that it now can\'t spell, which is rather unfortunate, but otherwise the image is very good. He still has his little hat, purple chair, and we\'ve got the window we asked for'

[13:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'along with the yellow optics. The next method uses the text in code create two node. If you want to use loads of images, then this is your node because it just keeps on growing. Four,'

[13:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'five, six, seven images, and it does masks as well. Apparently, though, they don\'t seem to work for me as it still appeared to see the whole image anyway. You can also change the megapixel size'

[14:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for the vision encoder and if the prompt is before or after yours. Whilst it doesn\'t have the individual token control of the previous node, you can use the native conditioning average'

[14:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as an alternative way to reduce the overall strength compared to your own prompt. Again, it can\'t spell too well, but we do have the chair, lovely hat, window, and his yellow optics.'

[14:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
